{"id":8955644,"docketId":66221859,"caseName":"Daniels v. Virginia","caseNameFull":"DANIELS v. VIRGINIA","slug":"daniels-v-virginia","docketNumber":"No. 485, Misc.","dateFiled":"1963-06-17","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1963,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Theodore J. St. Antoine for petitioners.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":1,"judges":"Carolina, City, Greenville, Harlan, Stated","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8946627,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1132,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"b550-8\">Per Curiam.</author>\n<p id=\"b550-9\">The motion for leave to proceed <em>in forma pauperis </em>and the petition for writ of certiorari are granted. The judgment is vacated and the case is remanded for further consideration in light of <em>Peterson </em>v. <em>City of Greenville, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9422598\"><a href=\"/opinion/106607/peterson-v-city-of-greenville/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Peterson v. City of Greenville\">373 U. S. 244</a></span>.</p>\n<judges id=\"Adl\">. Mr. Justice Harlan concurs in the result on the premises stated in his separate opinion in <em>Peterson </em>v. <em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9422598\"><a href=\"/opinion/106607/peterson-v-city-of-greenville/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Peterson v. City of Greenville\">City of Greenville</a></span> </em>and <em>Avent </em>v. <em>North Carolina, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9422598\"><a href=\"/opinion/106607/peterson-v-city-of-greenville/#248\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Peterson v. City of Greenville\">373 U. S., at 248</a></span>.</judges>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}